# ExaBGP qa/old/5.0/qa/encoding/unknown-message (ExaBGP 685f772e4e): .ci and .msg joined, options spelt option=
option=allowed:RFC 4271 Section 6.1 says of a message whose type is not recognized that "The Data field MUST contain the erroneous Type field", so ze sends Bad Message Type with the one octet 0xFF where 5.0 sent text, as ExaBGP 6.0 does (ExaBGP ALLOWED 5.0 unknown-message)
option=allowed-error:unexpected message = FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF0016030103FF;
option=file:unknown-message.conf
option=open:send-unknown-message
